  "title": "The Sidewalk Chalk Detour",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A volunteer wants visitors to avoid a pretend wet-paint mural on the floor, but a single STOP sign makes everyone bunch up. They add a clearly marked alternate path around the work area and an arrow back to the original route; traffic flows gently while the painter adds the final flower.",
  "hook": "Stopping is clear. Going somewhere else is missing.",
  "visible_action": "Figures halt at sign; queue grows; chalk arrows trace a loop; figures follow it; returning arrow joins the old route; painter finishes.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "When blocking a route, show a usable next option.",
  "gate": "Toy-scale staging only; real street closures, crowd routing, and accessibility require authorized planning and applicable standards.",
